; Runs as a SEPARATE "iris session" invocation, after the module install
; script (iris.script) has fully finished and that process has exited.
;
; This used to also set the _SYSTEM password here, but that turned out to
; have no effect on the real container: with Durable %SYS (ISC_DATA_DIRECTORY),
; %SYS -- including Security.Users -- is installed fresh the first time the
; container actually starts against an empty external volume, discarding
; whatever this throwaway build-time IRIS instance did to its own local %SYS.
; The password is now handled the supported way, via the iris-main
; entrypoint's --password-file flag (see compose.yaml "command" and the
; Dockerfile step that writes docker/.runtime-password.txt).
zn "MEUPORTAL"

; Building the image runs IRIS once inside the transient BuildKit sandbox
; container (hostname "buildkitsandbox"). Clearing any stamped hostname here
; is cheap insurance against IRIS showing a harmless "System appears to have
; failed over from node buildkitsandbox" warning on the portal.
Set tSC = ##class(MeuPortal.Installer).PrepareForContainerBundling()
Write !, "PrepareForContainerBundling: ", $Select(tSC=1:"OK", 1:$System.Status.GetErrorText(tSC))

halt
